1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,800
Swap hydrogen for deuterium in a
hydrogen-bonded crystal and, in our

2
00:00:03,820 --> 00:00:07,480
calculations, it leans toward the
polymorph with the shorter O-H bonds.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:13,860
Three machine-learned potentials get this
sign in 185 of 212 cases where the

4
00:00:13,880 --> 00:00:18,537
hydrogen bonds are moderate or strong, and
the rule says where it stops working.

5
00:00:18,557 --> 00:00:22,697
Polymorph energy gaps are smaller than any
machine-learned potential's error. So we

6
00:00:22,717 --> 00:00:27,537
compute only the isotope difference. Force
constants do not depend on mass, so one

7
00:00:27,557 --> 00:00:31,637
phonon calculation gives both hydrogen and
deuterium free energies, and the static

8
00:00:31,657 --> 00:00:37,014
gap cancels. Three universal potentials do
the work; SevenNet only votes on signs.

9
00:00:37,034 --> 00:00:42,714
We screened 220 polymorph pairs. The
isotope free-energy difference follows the

10
00:00:42,734 --> 00:00:49,554
change in mean O-H length, 0.11 to 0.13
meV per hydrogen per thousandth of an

11
00:00:49,574 --> 00:00:55,202
angstrom. The O-H stretch drives it, and
bending and libration cancel about half.

12
00:00:55,222 --> 00:00:59,442
Where hydrogen bonds are moderate or
strong, deuteration favours the polymorph

13
00:00:59,462 --> 00:01:06,362
with the shorter O-H bonds in 185 of 212
model evaluations. A baseline that always

14
00:01:06,382 --> 00:01:12,422
guesses one sign gets 131. Counted per
pair, 74 are right and 10 are wrong, and

15
00:01:12,442 --> 00:01:16,362
all 10 wrong pairs contain the same
aluminium hydroxide structure, where

16
00:01:16,382 --> 00:01:19,098
bending and libration outweigh the
stretch.

17
00:01:19,118 --> 00:01:24,238
With weak hydrogen bonds it fails, 2 of
20. We chose that boundary after seeing

18
00:01:24,258 --> 00:01:26,274
the data, and we say so.

19
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:30,874
Is this a shared model bias? Their O-H
stretch frequencies follow the slope

20
00:01:30,894 --> 00:01:36,134
measured from real mineral spectra, for O
to O distances between 2.5 and 2.8

21
00:01:36,154 --> 00:01:40,707
angstrom. That checks the main ingredient,
not the free energies.

22
00:01:40,727 --> 00:01:45,907
Diaspore turns into delta-AlOOH, a
possible deep-Earth water carrier. The

23
00:01:45,927 --> 00:01:51,307
measured boundary lies at higher pressure
and high temperature. Our 300 kelvin

24
00:01:51,327 --> 00:01:58,747
models put it at about 9 to 13 gigapascal,
and both say deuteration raises it, by

25
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:05,307
1.13 and 1.33 gigapascal. It is an
exploratory sign prediction, because

26
00:02:05,327 --> 00:02:11,205
delta-AlOOH has proton disorder there that
harmonic physics leaves out.

27
00:02:11,225 --> 00:02:14,445
Nobody has measured this directly, but the
isotope shift of a phase boundary equals

28
00:02:14,465 --> 00:02:18,865
the D/H fractionation between the two
phases, so deuterium partitioning between

29
00:02:18,885 --> 00:02:21,594
coexisting polymorphs is a direct test.

30
00:02:21,614 --> 00:02:24,480
An AI team ran the work.

31
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:32,890
Literature agents on Valency Bond pulled
the measured values and logged every

32
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,414
query.

33
00:02:38,184 --> 00:02:44,124
Predictions were committed to git before
the data were read. Councils of three

34
00:02:44,144 --> 00:02:48,704
models argued each claim, and every
decision records its dissent. A second

35
00:02:48,724 --> 00:02:52,266
model rewrote the calculation blind and
matched our numbers.

36
00:02:52,286 --> 00:02:57,186
Everything runs in an open marimo app.
Pick a pair and see the model numbers, the

37
00:02:57,206 --> 00:03:00,581
rule's call, and the Bond query behind
each measured value.

38
00:03:00,601 --> 00:03:07,401
Limits. One blind test came out mixed. The
physics is harmonic, with no proton

39
00:03:07,421 --> 00:03:11,881
tunnelling. The potentials are trained on
similar data, so three models agreeing is

40
00:03:11,901 --> 00:03:16,728
not three validations. Code, data and
every decision are public.
